It’s driven by your **user Cursor hooks**, not tmux itself.

### Config

`~/.cursor/hooks.json` runs the same script on two events:

```1:15:/Users/sinchunyeung/.cursor/hooks.json
{
  "version": 1,
  "hooks": {
    "beforeSubmitPrompt": [
      {
        "command": "./hooks/tmux-title.sh"
      }
    ],
    "stop": [
      {
        "command": "./hooks/tmux-title.sh"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

`tmux-title.sh` finds the real tmux pane for this process tree, then renames that window from whatever `tmux-title-summarize.py` prints.

### What the tab shows

| Event | Title |
|--------|--------|
| `beforeSubmitPrompt` | Short summary of your prompt (e.g. `Fixing foo`) |
| `stop` | `ready` / `aborted` / `error` from `status` |

On stop:

```190:192:/Users/sinchunyeung/.cursor/hooks/tmux-title-summarize.py
    elif event == "stop":
        status = data.get("status") or "done"
        print({"completed": "ready", "aborted": "aborted", "error": "error"}.get(status, "ready"))
```

Anything missing or unrecognized becomes **`ready`**.

### Why it can say `ready` while still working

There’s **no mid-turn update**. The title only changes on prompt submit and on `stop`. So once Cursor fires `stop` (turn ended, aborted, error, or sometimes when it yields for approval / a nested stop), the tab flips to `ready` and stays there even if the agent or a subagent is still going. The next `beforeSubmitPrompt` is what puts a working title back.

If you want, we can tighten this (e.g. only set `ready` for `status == "completed"`, ignore other stop payloads, or also hook `preToolUse` / `subagentStart` so the title stays “busy” while tools/subagents run).

input.old_string:
if event == "beforeSubmitPrompt":
    print(summarize_prompt(data.get("prompt") or ""))
elif event == "preToolUse":
    print(summarize_tool(data))
elif event == "subagentStart":
    print(summarize_subagent(data))
else:
    print("")

input.new_string:
if event == "beforeSubmitPrompt":
    print(summarize_prompt(data.get("prompt") or ""))
elif event == "preToolUse":
    print(summarize_tool(data))
elif event == "subagentStart":
    print(summarize_subagent(data))
elif event == "stop":
    status = data.get("status") or "completed"
    print({"completed": "ready", "aborted": "aborted", "error": "error"}.get(status, "ready"))
else:
    print("")
